From 93b54344c4b85603322df74bc06416c0897c0375 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/51] B70-V7-K4F: int8 KV prefill dequant without host reads
 (B70_PTH_FA_PREFILL_FAST=1)

K4 dequantised each sequence's blocks in a Python loop of 4-block slices per
layer after seq_lens/query_start_loc .tolist() (D2H syncs), then built the
remapped block table on the host. The builders now attach the scheduler's
host copies (query_start_loc_cpu, seq_lens_cpu_upper_bound) and K4F groups
from those, builds the scratch block table on the device with a uniform
per-group stride, and dequantises K and V of every referenced block in one
Triton launch per group. Same bytes as _dequant_blocks (bf16 roundings done
on the integer bits, RTNE); FA output equal to the stock loop. Falls back to
the loop with a log line when the host copies are missing.
---
 vllm/v1/attention/backends/b70_pth_fa.py  | 313 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 vllm/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py  |   3 +
 vllm/v1/attention/backends/triton_attn.py |   3 +
 3 files changed, 319 insertions(+)

